From 11ab9070650abd12a7f8f990e462d5d328f2fbd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5 (CLIVE engineering)" <claude-opus-5-5@clive.invalid>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:52:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Contain every decoder failure and echo nothing supplied in
 any refusal

Repairs the two material findings of the GPT exact-SHA review of
ca047b8963bcbf7124f71037a2fa14fc4853ab8d (activation successor 4), and
closes the same class one step further out.

F-01 parse_request turns every decoder failure into a refusal: besides
malformed UTF-8 and JSON, RecursionError (deep nesting) and ValueError
(integer beyond the digit limit), and the same around model validation.
The loop also contains any other unexpected intake failure as the fixed
INTAKE_UNAVAILABLE sentence and still ticks the Dispatcher, while
journal, lifecycle and store-conflict errors still stop it (fail closed).

F-02 The inbox directory is no longer operator input: the CLI flag is
removed, the config value must be one plain path component (refused
without echo), and receipts, outcomes and the projection name records
by the fixed label "requests/..." whatever the configured directory is.

Same class: intake refusals from the Objective door quoted rejected
values (e.g. an allowed path) into receipts and the public projection.
Refusal reasons now have every quoted literal and every supplied string
redacted; schema refusals redact supplied strings too.

17 new regression tests; each fails on ca047b89 and passes here.
Existing assertions unchanged. No protected path touched. Authored by
Claude Opus 5.5.
